# Revised 28 October 2026 by Sam Hedges
#
# Particle IDs conform to the 2017 revision of the
# Particle Data Group Monte Carlo Particle Numbering Scheme
# (see http://pdg.lbl.gov/2018/reviews/rpp2018-rev-monte-carlo-numbering.pdf)
#
# B(GT-) values for levels in 58Cu below 9 MeV were taken from :
# Y. Fujita, et al., Eur. Phys. J. A 13, 411–418 (2002). 
# Above 8.3 MeV, B(GT-) values were taken from:
# J. Rapaport et al., Nucl. Phys. A 410, 371–398 (1983).
# All B(GT-) values were multiplied by g_A^2 = (1.26)^2 to account for their 
# differing definition of B(GT-), which did not include that weak axial-vector 
# coupling constant. gA was assumed to have a value of 1.26 to conform with 
# T. N. Taddeucci et al., Nucl. Phys. A 469, 125–172 (1987).
#
# The B(F) value was taken as the sum-rule value g_V^2*(N_i - Z_i) with g_V=1,
# i.e. B(F) = 2.0, centered at the IAS. IAS value used was 0.20299 from ENSDF:
# <cite>
#
